-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Puncture, redesigned
-- ============================================================
-- "Puncture (2, 3): Redesigned.  Increases your Strength by 10/20/30% of your
--  Stamina. (3 ranks)"
--
-- What it was: -1/-2/-3 rage on Sunder Armor and Devastate.
--
-- Why this shape.  docs/prot_warrior_rage_audit.md flags Puncture (SS4 item 4)
-- as one of the cost reductions that is now overtuned: rage income was raised
-- but the flat cuts were never rescaled, so 3 points bought a larger share of a
-- smaller cost than intended.  Deleting the reduction outright fixes the rage
-- economy; replacing it with a Stamina-to-Strength conversion gives the tree a
-- point where stacking Stamina -- which a Protection warrior does anyway -- is
-- also its throughput scaling, instead of a talent that only mattered when
-- rage-starved.
--
-- Handled by DBC:
--   Everything except the amount.
--
--   EffectApplyAuraName1 = 29 SPELL_AURA_MOD_STAT
--   EffectMiscValue1     = 0 = STAT_STRENGTH
--   EffectBasePoints1    = 9 / 19 / 29, so $s1 renders 10 / 20 / 30 and the
--                          amount the script receives is 10 / 20 / 30.
--
--   The old SPELLMOD_COST plumbing is cleared: EffectMiscValue1 14 -> 0 and
--   EffectSpellClassMaskA1 16384 -> 0.  (The Devastate bit sat in effect 2's
--   mask, which is inert because Effect2 is 0.)
--
-- Handled by C++ (modules/world_of_alonecraft/src/WarriorProtConversions.cpp,
-- spell_warr_puncture):
--   The amount only.
--
-- Why a script at all.  Stat-to-stat has no aura either.  Aura 29 takes a flat
-- number of stat points, not a percentage of another stat, and
-- SPELL_AURA_MOD_RATING_FROM_STAT (220) only ever produces a *rating*.  So the
-- percentage is applied in DoEffectCalcAmount and refreshed on a heartbeat, the
-- same pattern as the weapon specialisations.
--
-- No circularity: the input is Stamina and the output is Strength, so the
-- conversion never feeds itself.
--
-- Spells:
--   12308 / 12810 / 12811 = Puncture ranks 1-3
-- ============================================================


